text:
When I write C I tend to always return any error code on the stack and pass the pointer to where I want the result to go. Makes managing memory easier. The owner gets to allocate.<p>Example:<p><pre><code>  #define E_DIVZERO -100
  float divide(int a, int b, int *result) { 
      if (b == 0) return E_DIVZERO;
      *result = a &#x2F; b;
  }</code></pre>
